ree market economy","price mechanism","Karl Marx"],"qpPage":6,"msPage":6,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["It was supported by Karl Marx","The price mechanism allocates all resources","There are no externalities","The state owns all the resources"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2024-jun-q3b","p":33,"section":"A","questionNumber":"3(b)","parentQuestion":"3","choiceGroup":null,"marks":3,"questionText":"Singapore is mainly a free market economy. The education system in Singapore produces some of the highest achieving students in international education rankings, with its teenagers coming top in tests in mathematics, reading and science. Singapore’s education system is provided by the state. With reference to the information above, explain why education is normally provided by the state.","topics":["1-3-2-externalities","1-3-4-information-gaps","1-1-6-types-of-economies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["state provision","education","positive externalities"],"qpPage":6,"msPage":6,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2023-jun-q1a","p":4,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(a)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"In a major reform of its command economy, the Cuban government will allow small private businesses to operate in most fields. Free market economists have long called for the role of small business to be expanded to help jump‑start the economy and to create jobs. With reference to the information provided, explain one advantage of a free market economy.","topics":["1-1-6-types-of-economies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["free market economy","command economy","Cuba"],"qpPage":2,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2023-jun-q1b","p":4,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(b)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"In a major reform of its command economy, the Cuban government will allow small private businesses to operate in most fields. Free market economists have long called for the role of small business to be expanded to help jump‑start the economy and to create jobs. Which one of the following economic thinkers supported the idea of a command economy?","topics":["1-1-6-types-of-economies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["command economy","Karl Marx","economic thinkers"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 1 as printed","type":"mcq","options":["Adam Smith","Friedrich Hayek","John Maynard Keynes","Karl Marx"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2023-jun-q5a","p":32,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(a)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"During the global health crisis, 11.7 million jobs were furloughed, costing the UK Government £70 billion. This meant people were paid by the government 80% of their wages even though they did not work. Some private sector employers continued to pay the remaining 20 %. With reference to the above information, define the term ‘mixed economy’.","topics":["1-1-6-types-of-economies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["mixed economy","definition","furlough"],"qpPage":8,"msPage":10,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2023-jun-q5c","p":32,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(c)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"During the global health crisis, 11.7 million jobs were furloughed, costing the UK Government £70 billion. This meant people were paid by the government 80% of their wages even though they did not work. Some private sector employers continued to pay the remaining 20 %. Which one of the following is a likely advantage of a command economy?","topics":["1-1-6-types-of-economies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["command economy","unemployment","furlough"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":11,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 5 as printed","ty